    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-09T21:21:53+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T21:21:53+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T10:51:53Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T10:51:53Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and trough currently over the centre of SA will gradually drift eastwards into Tuesday, clearing the border in the afternoon. A weak ridge of high pressure will develop south of the Bight on Wednesday, lingering into Thursday. A trough will then begin to move into the far west late Thursday, slowly drifting northeastwards across the state Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-09T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds north of Marla. Winds southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm with little or no rainfall. Winds southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 33.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly during the day then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending south to southwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
